  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat, on his v0.19.0 build): \"Simulator is not updating in realtime - the voxel body updates as the tool comes to the end of a G1 or G2 movement and not while its traveling using a detection of removal/collision whatever we wanna call it..\"\n\nWhat happens: during simulation playback the tool moves smoothly along a move, but the stock body is only cut when the tool reaches the end of that G1 or G2 move. On a long move the tool is seen travelling through uncut material, and the whole cut then appears at once.\n\nExpected: material is removed where the tool is, as it travels. The stock shown at any playback position is the stock cut up to that position (the part of the current move already travelled included), for lines and arcs alike.\n\nRules:\n- Display only: the verdicts (gouge, collision, rapid-in-stock) and what blocks the post must not change. They stay computed over whole moves as today; a partly shown move never hides or delays a finding.\n- Scrubbing backwards and jumping in the timeline still show the correct stock for that position.\n- Playback stays smooth on a large program (the partial cut of the current move must not re-cut the whole program each frame).\n\nDone means: a test steps playback to the middle of one long G1 and one G2 and reads the stock: material is removed up to the tool position and not beyond it; the end-of-program stock and every verdict are unchanged from before (pinned by the existing sim suites); scrubbing back restores the earlier stock.\n",
